    "updated_at": "2023-05-31T15:55:23Z",
    "body": "I was just writing that i'm not sure about `samp`, since it may refer to part of the UI or page that is translated.\r\n\r\nFwiw, `code` was excluded from auto-translation by Google and Yandex pretty much from the start.  I think it's the same for Bing, but i don't remember for sure.\r\n\r\nThis is, of course, not an exact science.  For example, putting translate=no around Unicode character names seems on the face of it a good idea, but actually they are usually translated for French readers (because the Unicode Consortium holds a set of code point name translations).  For example, recent translations of our i18n articles into french use the french Unicode names.\r\n\r\n",
